{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"28f23b1c29684f7fc0c9a8fbac0f084a278c7745ea5c81d8b9d662fe9a127da6","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate / relation snapshot reducer","key_entities":["plan-relation-snapshot-error","rebar review-plan",".tickets-tracker","plan_relation_snapshot","_store/event_append._prepare_event","tracker_head_sha","test_resign_tolerates_a_concurrent_writer_churning_tracker_temp_files"],"problem_keywords":["plan-relation reducer","event-less ticket directory","plan review indeterminate","store detritus","orphan directory"],"propositions":["A ticket directory with no CREATE or SNAPSHOT event causes the plan-relation reducer to error out, surfacing as INDETERMINATE verdict on unrelated tickets whose relation graph walks through it.","The error is invisible to git (git cannot track empty directories) and persists until manual removal, making existing broken clones unrepairable via pull.","The plan-relation reducer must tolerate event-less directories by skipping them with a warning naming the path, rather than failing the snapshot.","The writer-side fix (preventing directory creation before first event) is unsafe under concurrent store access and does not repair existing broken clones, so only reader-side tolerance is implemented."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787491897383535001,"uuid":"0310bf1c-1ce5-41c9-9a77-d3ea1d13bb00"}